na the state  oil company is is making plans to  purchase russian oil at lower costs  again because  you know higher prices in indonesia mean  that the government has to pay a lot for  subsidies and so it's purely an economic  decision to look for cheaper prices on  the market  now despite its heavy entanglement in  the commodities business indonesia also  wants to become carbon neutral by 2060  as we heard in the report uh possibly  sooner than 2060. how far along is the  country on this path  i would say  it's still it's still a long road indeed  um what we have heard  the ministry say is that  a new bill for new and renewable  energies is supposed to be passed by the  third quarter of this year which will  finally give a little bit more concrete  plans for how the energy transition is  going to be achieved  what has happened already is that  one or two of more utility scale solar  systems have come  um have have begun building i don't  think any of them have actually come  online yet  so it's really still very in the early  days and in my views  um  certain decisions for example to  actually um delay the rollout of the  carbon tax again which was supposed to  take effect this month but they have  said let's postpone it again for another  quarter three months or so those are all  signals that it is still very difficult  to  implement policies that could hurt the  traditional sectors journalist nadine  freischlad reporting from jakarta thank  you  you
 

